  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "C(m+n, r) = Σ_k C(m,k)·C(n,r-k) proved via Finset.powersetCard partition (LGV non-crossing contribution); lgvDet2 2×2 path matrix determinant defined; vandermonde_chu_from_lgv connects sequential LGV to Chu identity",
    "plain": "Connect the Lindström–Gessel–Viennot (LGV) lemma to Vandermonde-type identities. The standard Vandermonde identity C(m+n,r) = Σ_k C(m,k)·C(n,r-k) is the single-path degenerate case of LGV applied to Bool-vector lattice paths, where the 'non-crossing' condition holds trivially since there is only one path.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "Provides a combinatorial interpretation of Vandermonde via the LGV partition principle",
      "Establishes the 2×2 LGV path matrix and its determinant formula for lattice paths",
      "Identifies both standard Vandermonde (Bool-vector model) and Chu-Vandermonde (LGV e-function model) as instances of the same LGV framework",
      "Creates infrastructure connecting ballot problem results (BallotProblemOQ03) to binomial identities"
    ]
  },
